{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Coverage map at repository HEAD 8fa8f36b6482b2371128607a63c5483a9783e887.\\n\\n| Surface group | Exploration owner | Treatment | Inventory |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| Root client, governance, contributor, and harness documents | Shards A and B by audience | Full factual, taxonomy, prose, and link review | 10 root documents |\\n| Top-level docs pages | Shards A and B by audience | Full review with living guidance separated from history | 65 pages |\\n| Numbered ADRs plus ADR indexes | Shard A | Decision lifecycle, metadata, relationship, accuracy, and prose review | 103 artifacts |\\n| Design, research, calibration, experiment, archive, and migration material | Shard A | Lifecycle and provenance review. Maintained procedure receives prose review | 164 experiment assets plus related records |\\n| Infrastructure modules and runbooks | Shard A for documents and Shard C for embedded comments | Current-state, path, configuration, safety, and prose review | 14 documents |\\n| Examples and templates | Shard B for client text and Shard C for embedded comments | Portability, accuracy, completeness, synchronization, and prose review | 18 documents |\\n| CLI help sources | Shard B | Full command, option, behavior, discovery, and prose review | 55 files |\\n| Packaged explain guides | Shard B | Client-audience, portability, behavior, and prose review | 3 files |\\n| MCP registrar descriptions | Shard B | Tool discovery, parameter, behavior, error, and generated-reference review | All registered tools and the generated reference |\\n| Reviewer prompts | Shard C | Maintained prompt meaning and prose review with contract preservation | 87 files |\\n| Evaluation and workflow text | Shard C | Maintained specification and prose review with oracle preservation | 40 assets |\\n| Source Python | Shard C | Tokenized comment and docstring review plus registered presentation strings | 555 files |\\n| Script files | Shard C | Comment, help, diagnostic, and output review | 66 files |\\n| Test Python | Shard C | Comment and docstring review. Wording fixtures remain protected | 1,511 files |\\n| Workflow, configuration, Terraform, and related text | Shard C for embedded prose and Shard A for standalone runbooks | Operational rationale, current state, and presentation text review | 91 files |\\n| Schemas and structured descriptions | Shard C unless client-facing | Description-field review with key, enum, and contract preservation | All maintained schemas |\\n| Machine corpora, captures, wordlists, binary assets, and generated evidence | Root provenance check | Provenance, license, source, digest, and regeneration review. No line-level rewriting of frozen content | 156 machine-corpus assets plus binary and wordlist artifacts |\\n\\nUntracked dependencies, .git state, virtual environments, caches, and build output are outside the repository inventory. Generated documents are assessed through their canonical source and regeneration contract. Third-party license text remains verbatim. External captures, frozen model output, serialized fixtures, and wording-under-test cases remain immutable evidence. Their maintained wrappers, provenance metadata, labels, and explanatory text remain in scope. Technical identifiers, command syntax, code operators, schema keys, machine markers, and table separators remain outside prose replacement rules while the prose around them remains in scope.\\n\\nShard precedence prevents double counting. Client-facing strings belong to Shard B. Comments and docstrings belong to Shard C. Standalone internal records belong to Shard A. No project files changed."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787290780172350001,"uuid":"6e52c39e-4d93-4869-8143-130fbac14104"}